exports[`Unit 17 recorded output > 'substitution' > keeps the wording snapshot complete 1`] = `
"--- substitution · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   Solve this system by substitution.
display  coordinate-plane x -4..4/1 y -4..4/1 points [] lines [] "Coordinate plane, x-axis −4 to 4 by 1; y-axis −4 to 4 by 1" [system-substitution variables (x, y) equations [y = x − 3; −x + 3y = −7]]
answer   point (1, −2)
input    coordinate-plane
hint     Substitute the isolated expression into the other equation.
step 1   Start with the isolated equation.   [y = x − 3]
step 2   Substitute it into the other equation.   [−x + 3y = −7]
step 3   Solve for x, then use y.   [(1, −2)]
miss     coordinate-order-reversed = (−2, 1)   Enter x first, then y, in the stated order.
miss     vertical-direction-reversed = (1, 2)   Positive y moves up and negative y moves down.

