display  coordinate-plane x -6..6/1 y -6..6/1 points [] lines [] "Coordinate plane, x-axis −6 to 6 by 1; y-axis −6 to 6 by 1" [system-words frame pass-sales variables (x, y) prices 24/18 total 7 revenue 138 equations [x + y = 7; 24x + 18y = 138] "A community event sold 7 passes. Standard passes cost $24, and premium passes cost $18. Total sales were $138. Let x be standard passes and y be premium passes."]
answer   point (2, 5)
input    coordinate-plane
hint     Use the total count and total revenue as two equations.
step 1   Let x count standard and y count premium passes.
step 2   Write the total-count equation.   [x + y = 7]
step 3   Write the revenue equation.   [24x + 18y = 138]
step 4   Enter standard passes first, then premium.   [(2, 5)]
miss     coordinate-order-reversed = (5, 2)   Enter x first, then y, in the stated order.
miss     vertical-direction-reversed = (2, −5)   Positive y moves up and negative y moves down.

